# MIT colors for authentication UI

Auth pages and components under `src/app/[locale]/(auth)/` and `src/components/auth/` must follow the same palette as the public shell ([`src/styles/mit-theme.css`](src/styles/mit-theme.css)).

## Do

- **Submit / primary institute actions** (sign in, sign up, save password, save profile): use shadcn [`Button`](src/components/ui/button.tsx) with **`variant="mit"`** so CTAs stay **MIT web red** in both light and dark. (`variant="default"` follows theme `--primary`: neutral high-contrast in dark mode per [docs/mit-color-strategy.md](../../docs/mit-color-strategy.md).)
- **Fields**: [`Label`](src/components/ui/label.tsx) + [`Input`](src/components/ui/input.tsx) so borders, rings, and typography use **shadcn semantic tokens** (`border-input`, `ring-ring`, `text-foreground`).
- **Text links** (forgot password, sign up, sign in): use [`authInlineLinkClassName`](src/lib/mit-sailing/tokens.ts) or **`text-mit-red`** / theme utilities—not raw hex. See [mit-red-ink-usage.mdc](mit-red-ink-usage.mdc).
- **Rare non-`Input` fields:** [`authInputClassName`](src/lib/mit-sailing/tokens.ts) matches `Input` styling.
- **Informational banners** (non-error): prefer `bg-mit-red-highlight` + `text-foreground` over generic blue backgrounds.

## Do not

- Use **`blue-*`** Tailwind classes for auth buttons, links, or info banners.
- Paste **raw** MIT hex codes (`#750014`, `#ff1423`, etc.) in JSX or arbitrary Tailwind values—use theme utilities (`text-mit-red`, `bg-mit-red`, etc.) or [`tokens.colors`](src/lib/mit-sailing/tokens.ts) so values stay aligned with [`mit-theme.css`](src/styles/mit-theme.css). See [mit-brand-colors.mdc](mit-brand-colors.mdc).

See also [app-design-tokens-colors.mdc](app-design-tokens-colors.mdc) and [docs/mit-color-strategy.md](../../docs/mit-color-strategy.md).
